---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { buildSeo, languageLink } from "../../../lib/pages";

const path = "/douban-movie-rating/privacy/";
const alternatePath = "/zh/douban-movie-rating/privacy/";
const seo = buildSeo({
  title: "Douban Movie Rating Assistant Privacy Policy - Titpea",
  description:
    "How Douban Movie Rating Assistant handles film details, your optional OMDb key and its local rating cache.",
  path,
  alternatePath,
  locale: "en",
  ogImage: "/assets/og-douban-movie-rating.png",
});
---

<SiteLayout seo={seo} current="douban-movie-rating" locale="en" language={languageLink("en", alternatePath)}>
  <article class="privacy-page shell">
    <header class="privacy-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        <a href="/douban-movie-rating/">Douban Movie Rating Assistant</a>
      </p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: October 10, 2026</p>
      <p class="lead">
        Douban Movie Rating Assistant (豆瓣电影评分助手) is an unofficial Chrome extension that shows IMDb, Rotten
        Tomatoes and Metacritic ratings on Douban movie pages. It collects no personal information. It has no servers,
        no accounts, no analytics and no advertising.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-content prose">
      <section>
        <h2>What the extension reads</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Film details: on a film page (<code>movie.douban.com/subject/…</code>), it reads the title, year and IMDb ID
            shown on the page to look up ratings.
          </li>
          <li>
            Hover lookups: on other movie.douban.com pages, such as Top 250, charts and a film page's recommendations,
            it does nothing until you rest the pointer on a link to a film for about 0.3 seconds. It then fetches that
            film's Douban page from movie.douban.com and reads the same three details.
          </li>
          <li>It runs only on movie.douban.com and does not read any other website.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>What is sent, and to whom</h2>
        <p>
          Only to the OMDb API (<code>www.omdbapi.com</code>): the film's IMDb ID, or its title and year, together with
          an API key (the built-in shared key, or your own if you entered one). OMDb handles these requests under its
          own terms and policies. Nothing is sent to the developer or to anyone else.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each rating is a link. If you click one, your browser opens IMDb, Rotten Tomatoes or Metacritic with that
          film's IMDb ID or title in the address, as any link would.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Settings: whether the extension is on, and the OMDb API key you may choose to enter. Stored in Chrome sync
            storage (<code>chrome.storage.sync</code>), so Chrome Sync carries them between your own browsers if you
            have it on.
          </li>
          <li>
            Rating cache: results are kept in local storage (<code>chrome.storage.local</code>) for up to 7 days (1 day
            for films released in the last 90 days or not found on OMDb) so pages load faster.
          </li>
          <li>
            Request timestamps: while the shared key is in use, the times of the last minute's requests are kept locally
            to stay within its rate limit.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          When you open the toolbar popup, it checks whether the current tab is a Douban movie page to show its status.
          That check is not stored or sent.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
        <p>
          Clear the API key in the extension's settings to remove it. Uninstalling the extension removes all of its
          settings and cached data.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>What we never do</h2>
        <p>
          We do not collect names, email addresses, accounts or browsing history. We do not use remote code, analytics
          or trackers. Your data is not sold, transferred to third parties beyond the OMDb requests described above, or
          used for any purpose other than showing ratings.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Limited Use</h2>
        <p>
          Douban Movie Rating Assistant's use of information received from Chrome APIs adheres to the Chrome Web Store
          User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be published on this page with a new date.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:info@titpea.com">info@titpea.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
